---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About CoinAINews — Who We Are & Why We Write"
  description="CoinAINews is an independent crypto & AI news publication. Meet the team, learn how we report, and see what drives us."
  bodyClass="page"
  css="home-default"
  js="home-default"
  dir="ltr"
>
  <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:60px 20px;font-family:Poppins,sans-serif;">
    <h1 style="font-size:36px;font-weight:800;margin:0 0 24px;color:#111;">About CoinAINews</h1>

    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#444;margin-bottom:20px;">
      CoinAINews started with a simple frustration: crypto news had become exhausting to read. Every headline screamed "to the moon" or "it's over." Every article felt like it was written for traders, not for people trying to understand what was actually happening.
    </p>

    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#444;margin-bottom:20px;">
      So we built something different. A publication that treats you like an adult. That explains the context. That admits when things are unclear. That writes about crypto and AI the way you'd explain it to a friend who's smart but busy.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:32px 0 12px;color:#111;">Who we are</h2>

    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#444;margin-bottom:20px;">
      We're a small, independent team of writers, developers, and former traders. No venture capital. No hidden agenda. No sponsored articles disguised as news. Just people who've been in this space long enough to know what matters and what's noise.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:32px 0 12px;color:#111;">What we cover</h2>

    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#444;margin-bottom:20px;">
      Bitcoin, Ethereum, altcoins, stablecoins, wallets, market analysis, and crypto regulations — plus the growing overlap between blockchain and AI. If it's moving markets or shaping the industry, we're writing about it. If it's just hype, we're probably not.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:32px 0 12px;color:#111;">How we write</h2>

    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#444;margin-bottom:20px;">
      Every article is written by a human and reviewed before it goes live. We cite primary sources — on-chain data, official statements, court filings. When we share an opinion, we label it as one. When a story changes, we update it and note the change at the bottom.
    </p>

    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#444;margin-bottom:20px;">
      We don't publish price predictions. We don't tell you what to buy. We don't pretend to know what happens next. What we do is help you understand what's happening now — and why it matters.
    </p>

    <h2 style="font-size:22px;font-weight:700;margin:32px 0 12px;color:#111;">Why trust us</h2>

    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#444;margin-bottom:20px;">
      We're not perfect. We make mistakes. But when we do, we correct them publicly and quickly. We don't delete articles to hide errors. We don't take money to write positive coverage. And we don't pretend to be something we're not.
    </p>

    <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.8;color:#444;">
      Whether you've been in crypto since 2013 or just opened your first wallet yesterday, there's something here for you.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
